course: dictionary
lesson: 15
title: Serious words and trusted adults
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Abortion is a grown-up medical word. You may see it in health lessons, in the news or in books about big issues. It is a word to understand, but it is not one to guess at, so when you meet it, read the words around it for clues. «"Termination" is the official word for an abortion, ending a pregnancy on purpose.» The sentence gives you a gentler word that means the same thing, and it tells you that abortion means ending a pregnancy on purpose.
explain: Some serious words are discussed in different ways by different people. Your dictionary tells you what the word means, but families and communities can have strong and different views about it. If a word about health or the body makes you worried or confused, that is a good time to talk to a trusted adult, such as a parent, carer or teacher.
explain: Words can also have a second, rarer meaning. «Abort» means to stop something early, as in «abort the mission». The formal, rare meaning of abortion is a plan or attempt that fails and is stopped early. Check the context: is the sentence about health, or about a plan that has been stopped?
fact: Abortion is a medical operation or treatment that ends a pregnancy on purpose.
fact: «Termination» is the official word for an abortion.
fact: In formal or rare use, an abortion can mean a plan or attempt that fails and is stopped early.
fact: «Abort» means to stop something early, as in «abort the mission».
fact: People have strong and different views about abortion, so talk about it with a trusted adult if you have questions.
exercise: In «"Termination" is the official word for an abortion», which word is another name for abortion? | Glum | *Termination | Curt | Ancient
exercise: «The crew had to abort the mission when the engine failed.» What does abort mean here? | Win a prize | *Stop something early | Celebrate with a party | Start again from the beginning
exercise: Which is the formal, rare meaning of abortion? | A bright light that glows | A short, rude reply | A grey, wet day | *A plan or attempt that fails and is stopped early
test: Abortion is a medical word. If a word about health worries you or you are unsure what it means, what should you do? | *Talk to a trusted adult, such as a parent, carer or teacher | Repeat it loudly to your friends | Look for a word that rhymes with it | Guess and forget about it
test: Which word is a medical word for ending a pregnancy on purpose? | Curt | Famished | *Abortion | Dreich
exam: Which sentence uses abort in its older or technical sense? | The crew ate a big lunch together. | The crew sang songs on the bus. | *The crew had to abort the mission when the engine failed. | The crew wrote a long letter home.
